# LinuxCNC on a mill. Written from LinuxCNC's public G-code reference
# (linuxcnc.org/docs, "G-code" Quick Reference and the overview), no
# interpreter source.
#
# G21 is mm, G90 absolute, G94 units per minute. M3 turns the spindle on
# clockwise and M5 turns it off; S is the speed, written by the job.
# M2 ends the program. LinuxCNC reads nothing after M2, so M2 is the
# last line. A semicolon starts a comment for the rest of the line.
family = cnc
dialect = linuxcnc
send = file
features = spindle homing
start = G21 ; mm
start += G90 ; absolute
start += G94 ; mm per minute
start += M5 ; spindle off
end = M5
end += G0 Z5
end += G0 X0 Y0
end += M2 ; program end
